# UI conventions

## Match the neighborhood

- Copy patterns from nearby components (dialogs, search, shelves, clubs) instead of inventing new layout systems.
- Reuse existing primitives: `@/components/ui/*`, `BookCover`, `BookSearch`, shelf/club dialogs.
- Tabs for indentation; Biome formats — do not fight the formatter.

## Client vs server

- Default App Router pages/layouts are Server Components.
- Add `"use client"` only for hooks, browser APIs, or interactive widgets.
- Keep data fetching on the server when possible (`lib/**/queries.server.ts`, oRPC SSR client). Client mutations use `client` / `orpc` from `@/lib/orpc` + TanStack Query.

## UX patterns already in the app

- Debounced search (≥2 chars), `retry: false` for flaky Open Library calls.
- Dialogs that stay open for multi-add flows when that is the product intent.
- Owner-only controls gated by session / `isOwner`, not by hiding broken buttons for everyone.
- Toasts via `sonner` for mutation success/error.

## Routing / SEO

- Public indexable routes may need `app/sitemap.ts` updates — see `.cursor/rules/sitemap.mdc`.
- Catalog entities (OL works/authors) use on-demand metadata; do not enumerate the whole OL catalog in the sitemap.
